/**
 * PostToolUse Tool Dispatcher: every ork PostToolUse handler in one process.
 *
 * yellow-refactor M1, phase 2. Live on CC 2.1.316 an Edit starts 14 ork
 * PostToolUse processes and a Bash 8 (docs/hook-process-measurements/
 * 2026-10-31-main-live.json). This handler runs the same handlers in one
 * process.
 *
 * OFF by default: wired only into the flag variant written by
 * scripts/unified-pretool-hooks.mjs, which keeps every PostToolUse group
 * matcher and points each at this one identical command. CC launches an
 * identical command once per event, so a call any group matches starts one
 * process, and a call no group matches starts none, exactly as today.
 *
 * Routing: POSTTOOL_GROUPS mirrors the shipped PostToolUse groups (a test
 * asserts deep equality), matched the way CC matches: empty or "*" is every
 * tool, identifier characters and "|" are an exact list, anything else is an
 * unanchored regex (CC changelog: hyphenated identifiers exact-match).
 *
 * Merge, as CC merges parallel hooks of one event:
 * - additionalContext and systemMessage from every handler are joined
 *   (an async handler's output used to arrive after the call; now it arrives
 *   with it).
 * - Only a handler that was sync may block (decision:'block', continue:false)
 *   or replace tool output (updatedToolOutput / updatedMCPToolOutput); an
 *   async one never could, because CC had already moved on.
 * - Each handler is isolated: a throw is logged and the rest still run.
 */

